\e[1m\e[38;2;207;173;0mWhat the tools cost\e[0m\e[0m

The \e[1mread\e[0m tool is cheap and \e[38;2;192;128;80mbash\e[0m is not, so the \e[3morder\e[0m matters. A run looks like this:

\e[38;2;201;166;212mfunc\e[0m \e[38;2;129;162;190mmain\e[0m() {
    fmt.\e[38;2;129;162;190mPrintln\e[0m(\e[38;2;181;189;104m"hello"\e[0m)
}

\e[38;2;192;128;80m• \e[0mread first, and read widely
\e[38;2;192;128;80m• \e[0mrun only what the reading could not answera nested point, to show the indent

Tool\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mWhat it does\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mCost
read\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mtakes a file and hands it back\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m1
grep\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mwalks the tree looking for a pattern\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m4
bash\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mruns a command in a sandbox with no network\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m40

\e[38;2;150;152;150m\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150mThe costs are made up, and the table is here to be watched as it draws.\e[0m

See \e[38;2;129;162;190mthe notes\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150m (https://example.com/notes)\e[0m for the rest.

